            <note corresp="#d150-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d150-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives and Records Administration, RG 59, Central Files 1964-66, POL
                    10 PORT. Confidential; Priority. Drafted by Barbour; cleared by
                        Williams, Sisco, and Buffum; and approved by Burdett. Pouched to Luanda, Lourenco Marques,
                    and USUN.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d150-f2" n="2" xml:id="d150-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 778 from Lisbon, April 10, reported that Anderson had requested a meeting with Salazar. (Ibid., POL 15-1 PORT)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d150-f3" n="3" xml:id="d150-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 764 from Lisbon, April 3, reported on Anderson’s talks with Noguiera on Portuguese Africa. Anderson visited Angola February 29-March 10,
                    and Mozambique March 10-19, 1964.</p>
            </note>
